  "tree_id": 1498,
  "family": "Magnoliaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Michelia champaca &lt;/em&gt;is an evergreen tree valued for its ornamental and highly fragrant blooms. Its glossy, vibrant green foliage provides a lush canopy. From mid-winter to early summer, elegant flowers emerge with thin, waxy, yellowish-orange tepals and a sweet, citrus-like aroma. Popular across tropical to subtropical gardens, this species attracts both hummingbirds and butterflies. Its fruits burst open at maturity, dispersing bright red seeds. It is very sensitive to frost.&nbsp;",
