  "california_native": 0,
  "ethnobotanical_info": "Golden Champaca holds reverence in Buddhist temples and ceremonies. The flowers produce essential oils used for fine perfumes. Its fruit is edible, while its durable wood is used for buildings, furniture, cabinetry, carvings, and turnery. This species is applied in traditional medicines to treat leprosy, colic, dry skin, and bacterial infections.",
